================================================================================================================================================
Spring Boot runs on top of the JVM; it doesn't own the garbage collector.

You select the collector using JVM startup options, typically through the command line, 
Docker/Kubernetes environment variables, or deployment configuration.

For your Java 21 Spring Boot services, I'd use G1 as the initial baseline, 
observe the workload, and only move to ZGC/Parallel/Serial when the application's actual latency, 
throughput, heap, and CPU characteristics justify it.

